.TH DANBY-LOGISTICPREDATORS 1
.SH NAME
danby-logisticpredators \- logistic regulation of prey and predators
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/logisticpredators
.SH MODEL
X' = rX(1-X/K)-aXY;
Y' = Y(cX-d)(1-Y/L).
.PP
K limits prey in the absence of predators and L limits predator growth.
The positive intersection X=d/c, Y=r(1-X/K)/a is marked.  A second predator
nullcline at Y=L makes it possible to compare regulation of only the prey with
regulation of both populations.
.SH DISPLAY
Phase and time plots update together as any of the six coefficients changes.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag the phase portrait to set initial populations and the bottom tracks to
set r, K, a, c, d, and L.  Space pauses, period steps, r resets, and q exits.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/logisticpredators.b
.br
.B /appl/temple/logisticpredators.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danby-logisticprey (1),
.IR numerics (2)
